{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the gathering of the waters He called Seas.</b> The name 'sea' is not applied to the waters but to the excavation, and this is what Onkelos translated: ולבית כנישות מיא — that is, the excavation which is the gathering-place where the waters are gathered. And thus Scripture says (Isaiah 11:9): ״כמים לים מכסים״ — for the waters cover the excavation called 'sea'; and likewise in the blessing of the fish or the taninim on the fifth day, it says ״ומלאו את המים בימים״ — explaining that the waters stand in the seas. A further proof is the Sea that Solomon made, of which it is written (II Kings 7): ״ואת הים הוריד מעל הבקר״. And it says ״קרא ימים״ — 'Seas' — and not 'Sea,' because they are many; and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that they are seven seas:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:24:43.929752845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}